// madc -i: D10's show of a UTF-8 string (plan §41.4a; found building
// §41.7a's slice 1). The text, entered again, yields the value, and a
// well-formed UTF-8 sequence is written as itself, as Julia and Python show
// a string; a byte outside one stays an octal escape. gcc 13 and clang 18
// read "été" and "\303\251t\303\251" as the same five bytes (strcmp 0,
// strlen 5 and 5), and so does madc.
#include <string.h>
const char *s = "été";
